{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And He said to Aaron: Take you a calf, a young bull, for a sin-offering.</b> To make atonement for the deed of the Calf, concerning which it is written (Exodus 32) that Aaron made." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> 'Take you a calf' — why did it not say 'Take you a bull (פר)' but 'Take you a calf (עגל)'? Because through a calf the priesthood was made unstable in your hand, and through a calf it is established in your hand."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:08.772392285Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}